body:
| Q                   | A
| --------------------| ---------------
| PHPUnit version     | 8.0.6
| PHP version         | 7.3.3
| Installation Method | PHAR scoped

Using Prophecy `TypeToken` causes some problems when using the scoped PHAR. Running the same test with the regular PHAR of the same version does not cause any exception or failure.

**Source classes:**
```
namespace App;

class ServiceToMock
{
    public function performAction(string $string): void
    {
    }
}
```

```
namespace App;

class MyService
{
    /**
     * @var ServiceToMock
     */
    private $serviceToMock;

    public function __construct(ServiceToMock $serviceToMock)
    {
        $this->serviceToMock = $serviceToMock;
    }

    public function doSomething(): void
    {
        $this->serviceToMock->performAction('Some string');
    }
}
```


**Test case:**
```
namespace App\Tests;

use App\MyService;
use App\ServiceToMock;
use PHPUnit\Framework\TestCase;
use Prophecy\Argument\Token\TypeToken;

final class MyServiceTest extends TestCase
{
    public function testDoSomething(): void
    {
        $mock = $this->prophesize(ServiceToMock::class);

        $mock->performAction(new TypeToken('string'))
            ->shouldBeCalledOnce();

        $subject = new MyService($mock->reveal());

        $subject->doSomething();
    }
}
```


